# Components and Styling

## Component Rules

- Use PascalCase files in `components/`.
- Prefer named exports for reusable components.
- Keep one clear responsibility per component.
- Type props with `interface` and avoid implicit `any`.
- Reuse existing shared UI before creating near-duplicate variants.

## Import Order

1. external packages
2. alias imports (`@/...`)
3. relative imports (`./...`)

## Tailwind Rules

- Use utility-first classes in JSX; avoid unnecessary CSS modules.
- Use `clsx` for conditional classes, not manual string concatenation.
- Keep responsive classes mobile-first (`sm`, `md`, `lg`).
- Preserve existing visual language: rounded sections/cards, soft shadows, gray backgrounds, green orange.
- For reusable colors/surfaces, define or reuse semantic tokens in `app/globals.css` via `@theme inline` and consume classes like `text-ink`, `bg-orange`, `text-body-muted`.
- Avoid repeating arbitrary color utilities (`text-[#...]`, `bg-[#...]`, `bg-[rgba(...)]`) across components; keep arbitrary values only for true one-off visuals.

## Global CSS

- Keep custom CSS minimal and centralized in `app/globals.css`.
- Define design tokens via CSS variables and Tailwind `@theme inline`.
- Avoid adding component-specific complex styles in global CSS.

## Accessibility Basics

- Use semantic layout elements and heading order.
- Ensure clear focus/hover behavior for interactive controls.
- Use meaningful `alt` text for all images.
